+# Privacy implementation and third-party audit
+
+Reviewed November 6, 2026. Scope: all published HTML/CSS, client execution,
+resource requests, runtime dependencies, HTTP responses, and data clearing.
+
+## Inventory and decisions
+
+| Item | Before | Current behavior |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| Hero photo | Browser requested images.unsplash.com, disclosing IP and request metadata | Same photo downloaded once and served at /assets/coffee-hero.jpg; no visitor request to Unsplash |
+| Fonts | System fonts | System fonts; no font service |
+| JavaScript, analytics, embeds | None | None; CSP blocks all scripts, frames and outbound connections |
+| Runtime server | Unpinned statikk download on start | Node built-ins only; no package download or third-party runtime code |
+| Browser data | None created | No cookies, storage, fingerprinting, identifiers or profiles |
+| Forms | None | Bodyless POST to /logout only asks the browser to clear origin data; no form fields |
+| Logs | Host-dependent | Application records no request URLs, headers, IPs or bodies; hosting logs require separate review |
+
+Original photo source:
+https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1495474472287-4d71bcdd2085?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1350&q=80
+
+Keep the photo local when updating it. No SRI/CORS exception is needed because
+there are no external subresources. This is a technical source audit, not an
+independent vendor certification. No browser/network inspection was performed.
+
+## Serving and deployment
+
+Run `npm run build` for the static privacy audit and deployable `dist/` directory.
+Run `npm start` (or `node dist/server.mjs` from the repository root) when deploying.
+The Node server is necessary: HTML meta tags cannot enforce Permissions-Policy,
+frame-ancestors, HSTS or Clear-Site-Data. A generic static host does not reproduce
+these protections or the clearing endpoint automatically.
+
+Terminate production traffic with HTTPS at a trusted reverse proxy. Set
+`PUBLIC_ORIGIN=https://your-real-domain` behind that proxy so the clearing endpoint
+can verify the full request origin. The proxy must preserve the security headers
+on every response, including errors and redirects. Do not enable access logging
+without documenting a necessary purpose, redaction, restricted access and a
+short retention period. Never log query strings, credentials or form bodies.
+Review the provider's IP/security logs and deletion settings before release.
+
+HSTS starts at 300 seconds to avoid locking an unverified domain into a long
+policy. Increase after HTTPS is validated; subdomains/preload are intentionally
+excluded until every affected host is reviewed. CSP violation reporting is
+disabled to avoid collecting URLs or script snippets unnecessarily.
+
+The server publishes only an explicit file allowlist, sends no-store on all
+responses and does not reflect request data in error messages. Request bodies are
+not parsed or saved. New data collection needs server validation, size limits,
+rate limits, purpose-specific retention/deletion and a nearby explanation. If
+authentication is added, use server-managed `__Host-` session cookies with
+Secure, HttpOnly, SameSite=Lax and Path=/; invalidate the server session on logout.
+There are no accounts or server sessions to invalidate in this version.
+
+The clearing endpoint accepts same-origin POST requests only and redirects home
+with Clear-Site-Data for cookies, storage and cache. It clears the entire origin,
+so use a dedicated origin. It depends on browser support and secure delivery;
+the application never claims that it erases hosting-provider records. Account,
+menu and ordering routes remain the original placeholders.
+
+## Continuing review
+
+Run the build for every resource or dependency change. Its conservative source
+audit rejects scripts, third-party URLs, inline code, embeds, personal-data fields,
+new forms and dependencies until explicitly reviewed. CSP separately blocks
+unauthorized execution and network connections at runtime. This source gate is
+not a full HTML parser, vulnerability scanner or replacement for release review.
+
+Before approving any new vendor, record its purpose, data received (including IP,
+referrer and cookies), subprocessors, retention/deletion terms and owner here.
+Prefer self-hosting or a local facade. If an external immutable script/style is
+necessary, pin its version and integrity digest, omit credentials, suppress the
+referrer and update the CSP deliberately. Never persist sensitive data or tokens
+in browser storage. Re-audit before each release and whenever vendors change.
